 *
 * - Every payload is a plain object — no functions, no `Symbol`,
 *   nothing that survives `structuredClone` only by accident.
 * - `payload` is best-effort metadata. Hosts must branch on
 *   `(event, code)` first; payload fields are advisory.
 * - The widget never sends the session token back to the host: the
 *   token rides one-way on the launch URL only. Inbound `postMessage`
 *   payloads are *not* schema-filtered for token-shaped keys — the
 *   parser validates only that `event` is a non-empty string and
 *   forwards the rest verbatim. What makes inbound messages safe is the
 *   `event.source` + `event.origin` gating in `client/widget`, not a
 *   payload strip.
